<!-- MC-PATCH: mc-toolbar-loader-rc56.8 -->
<!-- MC-PATCH: mc-back-button-rc53.4 -->
<!-- Lesson 978 (rc56.8): MiracleClaw chat toolbar (Attach / Secrets / Voice
     / Modules). Loaded as a single self-contained IIFE that gates on
     `window.location.host === '127.0.0.1:28789'` so it only mounts when the
     openclaw chat page is hosted by MC's Tauri webview. The script
     injects its own CSS via `<link>` and creates its own floating panel +
     dropdowns + modals, all class-prefixed `mc-oc-` so they cannot collide
     with the openclaw host page. See depot/openclaw-patches/dist/control-ui/
     mc-toolbar.{js,css} for the implementation.

     The mc-back-button patch (Lesson 502/511) was previously appended
     directly to index.html; we moved it here so all control-ui additions
     share the same idempotent insertion path (Lesson 511) and so the
     bundle-runtime.sh re-extract pipeline wipes them all together. The
     markers below let the patcher skip if either piece is already present. -->
<script defer src="./mc-back-button.js"></script>
<script defer src="./mc-toolbar.js"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./mc-toolbar.css" />
<!-- rc57.25: calendar overlay (month grid + event editor). Loaded BEFORE
     mc-toolbar is fine either way since both are `defer` (execute in
     document order), so this must stay AFTER mc-toolbar.js only in the
     sense that the button reads window.McCalendar lazily at click time.
     Kept last so the toolbar's DOM mounts first. -->
<script defer src="./mc-calendar.js"></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./mc-calendar.css" />
